    "choi-source-issue": {
      "path": "/private/tmp/cmm-round67-choi-issue.json",
      "sha256": "122e1e28274336068c19c7a6ca8c51529000474e4beb5c7fd5ae1c5e8243f294",
      "result": {
        "body": "The Choi et al. (2023) study, DOI [10.1128/aem.02048-22](https://doi.org/10.1128/aem.02048-22), supports narrow crocidolite-associated iron reduction and a chrysotile assay with no demonstrated magnesium/silicon release enhancement. These are not recovery or detoxification claims. The full PMC main text and all four original figures were inspected; the official supplement remains unavailable through tested routes.\n\nThe missing artifact is `aem.02048-22-s0001.pdf`, linked by the [publisher](https://journals.asm.org/doi/suppl/10.1128/aem.02048-22/suppl_file/aem.02048-22-s0001.pdf) and [PMC](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/10304897/bin/aem.02048-22-s0001.pdf). Publisher requests returned 403, PMC download routes returned challenge pages, and EuropePMC reports the article outside its open-access subset. A browser surface was unavailable. These are access limits, not evidence that the file does not exist.\n\nFollow-up work:\n\n- Acquire the original supplement through a legitimate accessible route, verify file identity and record its checksum, version and reuse terms. Inspect its recipes, Tables S1-S4, Figures S1-S11 and extraction/beam controls before adopting additional quantitative claims.\n- Reconcile chrysotile Results values (Mg 1.6 ± 0.11 mM in cultures and 0.87 ± 0.63 mM in medium alone) with Figure 2B bars and the stated 0.69 ± 0.08 mM inoculum correction. Determine which time point, background and correction each number uses; do not silently replace a figure or text value.\n- Clarify Methods' statement that ICP-OES values subtract negative-control measurements, given separately displayed mineral-medium control series. Recover the exact blank/control definitions and calculation basis.\n- Verify sample composition, preparation and extraction fractions without converting HCl-extractable Fe(II)/total-Fe fractions into recovered-metal yield. Resolve structural versus surface-coating iron only if additional evidence supports it.\n- Save successor scientific reviews if new evidence materially changes `chrysotile.yaml` or `riebeckite.yaml`; preserve current observations and append history.\n\nThe narrow records retain these limitations. This issue tracks source acquisition and interpretation, not a known blocking defect in their qualitative accepted claims. No contact with authors is authorized by this issue itself.\n",
        "number": 210,
        "state": "OPEN",
        "title": "Acquire Choi 2023 supplement and reconcile asbestos assay controls",
        "url": "https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CMMMech/issues/210",
        "recorded_at": "2026-10-14T09:26:45.973603+00:00",
        "body_sha256": "0f50b1c47c7cda2c429e7d0997362ea0502d7cea1f897692ee332574fd1db32e"
      }
    },
